# Capstone 2 – Personal Portfolio Website

## 📌 Project Overview

Capstone 2 is a personal portfolio website developed as part of my full-stack web development learning journey. Building on the foundational HTML skills practiced in Capstone 1, this project introduces CSS styling, Bootstrap components, and website navigation to create a more visually appealing and user-friendly experience.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- **HTML5** – Structures the webpage and organizes content.
- **CSS3** – Customizes colors, fonts, spacing, and layout.
- **Bootstrap** – Provides prebuilt styling, layout utilities, and responsive design components.

## ✨ Features

- Personal profile and portfolio information
- Navigation bar with clickable links
- Custom styling using CSS
- Bootstrap components and layout utilities
- Links to additional projects and portfolio pages
- Organized webpage sections

## 🎯 Learning Objectives

- Build on foundational HTML knowledge
- Apply CSS styling to improve webpage appearance
- Practice using Bootstrap for page layouts and components
- Create functional navigation menus using hyperlinks
- Improve webpage organization and user experience
- Develop front-end web design skills

## 📂 Project Type

**Front-End Web Development | HTML, CSS & Bootstrap Capstone Project**

## 📚 Project Status

✅ Completed

## 🚀 Project Progression

**Capstone 1:** Basic personal profile webpage built with HTML.

**Capstone 2:** Expanded personal website incorporating CSS, Bootstrap, navigation menus, and additional styling techniques.

This project demonstrates my progression from creating basic HTML webpages to building more structured and styled websites.
